{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","type":"heading","text":"The Snapshot Pattern","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"State(observer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" macro generates a separate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Explicit equality guards (","type":"text"},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are unnecessary. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already checks equality on ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if more than 100 changes are drained within a single debounce interval (the "},{"code":"loopThreshold","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter; 250 ms by default). It counts only dispatches that changed an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and it reports once per burst — the count starts over after a whole debounce interval with no drains. This usually means an effect or plugin dispatches an action on every state change, feeding the cycle it reacts to. A steady stream of edits, such as a slider drag, stays well under the threshold and is not reported."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Debounced-Persistence","type":"heading","text":"Debounced Persistence","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drain restarts the flush’s debounce timer, so a burst of edits is written once. The timer is never pushed further than "},{"code":"maxWait","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" past the oldest pending change (four debounce intervals, and at least a second, by default), so continuous edits still reach storage while they continue. A retry of a failed flush keeps its own schedule; a new edit postpones it only when the flush it schedules is due first and carries the failed batch anyway."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","type":"heading","text":"Effect Threading","level":2},{"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Blocking calls (","type":"text"},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"terminationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"code":"waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Task.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"code":"Data(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","anchor":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"title":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Design Principles","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"title":"Security Posture","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"topic"}}}